WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.371 --> 00:00:01.710
(gentle violin music)

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:04.860
- Traditional Hasidic music
is based on words of prayer.

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:07.640
It has a certain sadness to it.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.427
But my music is different.

00:00:09.427 --> 00:00:11.136
♪ Instead of searching Google, ♪

00:00:11.136 --> 00:00:12.563
♪ I'm busy making Kugel ♪

00:00:12.563 --> 00:00:15.965
("Hang Up the Phone" by Lipa Schmeltzer)

00:00:15.965 --> 00:00:18.870
I was the first one with
the whole Hasidic outfit,

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:21.870
that come from a very
close-minded community,

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:25.474
who went to do crazy
shows with crazy outfits.

00:00:25.474 --> 00:00:30.190
("Hang Up the Phone" by Lipa Schmeltzer)

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:32.820
I've been called the Hasidic Lady Gaga.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:35.070
I've been called the Jewish Elvis.

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:38.280
But I promise you, I
would rather be just Lipa.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:41.530
(intense techno music)

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:45.160
This is the house I grew up.

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:46.820
Twelve children in this house.

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:49.670
I was born in New Square,
a religious orthodox,

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:51.440
very close-minded community.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.420
We had no radio, no television,

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:54.715
there's only one rabbi, one synagogue,

00:00:54.715 --> 00:00:57.930
one girls' school, one boys' school.

00:00:57.930 --> 00:01:00.500
I barely left the community.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:02.220
I was having a hard time as a child,

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:04.320
and traditional Hasidic
music was something

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:05.470
that gave me an outlet.

00:01:06.999 --> 00:01:08.090
(singing)

00:01:08.090 --> 00:01:10.140
I only did Hasidic music originally,

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:11.930
so I started to perform only at weddings.

00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:14.540
That was my dream, to be a wedding singer.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:17.060
I had to be 21 years old when I heard

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:18.990
my first non-Jewish song.

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:21.160
I started working for the
butcher in the fish store,

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:22.740
so I put the radio on.

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:23.760
And I think the first song was

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:26.080
♪ I need to know, ohhh I need to know ♪

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:28.690
♪ Tell me baby girl,
'cause I need to know. ♪

00:01:28.690 --> 00:01:31.101
And that opened up a whole world to me.

00:01:31.101 --> 00:01:33.461
♪Sorry, gotta go party,
so you can join me ♪

00:01:33.461 --> 00:01:35.232
♪ In my Ferrari, hey! ♪

00:01:35.232 --> 00:01:37.649
(funky beat)

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:40.470
Listening to sexy music, I had a chance

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:42.200
and discovered there's a different way

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:45.220
of composing lyrics and composing music.

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:47.260
So when I started writing lyrics,

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:49.550
the lyrics that I used were new.

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:53.320
My music was advancing towards hip-hop,

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:55.973
R&amp;B, and American modern music.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:02:01.110
My music has, had many
reactions throughout the years.

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:03.480
Many rabbis tried to stop me.

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:06.130
Everything that's new can make some people

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:08.850
who live in a fanatic
system, can make them mad.

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:12.100
But many good people,
even rabbis, love me,

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:14.890
and they recognize that
this is God-given talent,

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:16.240
and they don't let me stop.

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:20.050
I was privileged to
perform in crazy places,

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:21.880
I did one show even with Jay Leno!

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:24.170
I did Madison Square Garden.

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:26.890
I've made music videos that
have millions of views.

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:29.410
I've recorded probably, 19 albums or so.

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:32.386
I'm never stopping until
God will say, “Lipa is done.”

00:02:32.386 --> 00:02:34.900
(intense techno music)

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:38.130
I have many times, I was
thinking to drop out completely

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:40.500
from the Hasidic community, just run away.

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:42.060
But this is where I
was born, this is where

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:44.770
my heritage is, this is
where my upbringing is.

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:48.710
And it's a smarter move to
take this and modernize it.

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:51.660
I try to take Hasid and then open it up.

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:53.638
It's a beautiful thing to open the mind.

00:02:53.638 --> 00:02:55.198
(inhales loudly)

00:02:55.198 --> 00:02:56.031
I think.

